    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0888" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg880"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.24/1750</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Jacques J.
                            Reinstein, Assistant to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-22">September 22, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Restrictions on Japanese Trade and Payments in the
                        British Empire</hi>
                </p>
                <p>All British countries have frozen Japanese assets. According to the British
                    Embassy, all have agreed in principle to the policy adopted <pb facs="0889"
                        n="881" xml:id="pg881"/> by the British Government of restricting exports to
                    Japan to the minimum level necessary to obtain essential imports from Japan.</p>
                <p>As a practical matter trade between the British Empire and Japan is virtually at
                    a standstill. Except for manganese and iron ore from Malaya and cotton from
                    India, exports to Japan of products valuable from a military viewpoint have been
                    completely cut off.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">acques</hi>] J. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">einstein</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
